From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 07:11:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lib/api: let a GUI change answer before the listener restarts

A change to the GUI settings restarts the GUI/API listener. The restart
gives in-flight requests shutdownTimeout (100 ms) and then closes their
connections. The request that made the change is still in flight: after
the change is committed it saves config.xml. When saving takes longer
than 100 ms (slow storage, busy device) the client gets EOF instead of a
response, although the change was applied and saved.

Count the requests that may change the config from the moment they
arrive, and let the restart wait until they have answered. The restart
signal no longer blocks, because the request that caused it is now
waited for; a restart already pending picks up a later change.
---
 lib/api/api.go              |  62 +++++++++++++++++-
 lib/api/api_restart_test.go | 126 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 185 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 lib/api/api_restart_test.go

